E('ngocdolang','1969-05-17','May 17–23','Ngọc Dơ Lang range. In Đắk Tô 2, the Front\'s forces surround and badly hurt the Saigon 22d Ranger Battalion.','121',also=OP,place='ngoc-do-lang',see='cal.1969-05-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Đắk Tô 2: Ranger Battalion 22 surrounded')
E('plt668','1969-05-24','May 24','Plây Thông Breng, Hill 668. In Đắk Tô 2, Battalion 9 of the 66th Regiment hurts the 2d Battalion of the Saigon strike force: over 300 out of action. About then 250 of its 1st Battalion are put out of action. The history calls it the campaign\'s best result.','121',also=OP,place='plei-thong-breng',see='cal.1969-05-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Plây Thông Breng, Hill 668: Battalion 9 hurts a strike battalion')
E('h875','1969-05-31','May 31','Hill 875. In Đắk Tô 2, the 66th Regiment and Battalion 3 of the 28th close round the Saigon 11th and 23d Ranger Battalions on the hill and attack in turn; hundreds out of action. The Saigon command pulls back to call air and artillery, the attackers close up each time. The history notes that Regiment 174 beat the American 173d Airborne\'s 2d Battalion on the same hill, Nov. 1967.','121–22',also=OP,place='hill-875',see='cal.1969-05-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Hill 875: Rangers surrounded by Regiment 66')
C('cal.1969-05-11.vietnam-hanoi','121–22, 127','Đắk Tô 2 to its close: June 26, 4,135 out of action, 88 vehicles and 103 aircraft destroyed, hundreds of prisoners; the history names the new tactic of continuous encirclement and attack, "bao vây tiến công liên tục", first used here, its figures its own; the summer phase May 11–June 20: 29 battalions and equivalents put out of action, in Central Trung Bộ 150 strategic hamlets and 90 resettlement areas broken, 200,000 people freed','D-E')
E('apache','1969-05-10','May 10–11','A Lưới–A Bia valley, west of Huế. The American and Saigon commands decide on Apache Snow: five battalions, the 1st, 2d and 3d of the 187th Brigade, 101st Airborne, and two of the Saigon 1st Division. The 3d Battalion, Lt. Col. Weldon Honeycutt, searches round A Bia from posts at Hills 337 and 1,087, and is ambushed on the saddle north of the mountain: dozens out of action.','123–24 and n. 1',also=OP,place='a-bia',us=True,check='the day of the decision, May 10, and of the ambush, May 10–11; the history gives "ngày 10-5-1969" for the first and "các ngày 10 và 11-5" for the second.',lw='Apache Snow opens at A Bia')
E('abia12','1969-05-12','May 12','A Bia. In the morning B-52s and other bombers carpet the mountain. Three companies of the 3d Battalion, 187th, move north in several columns into Regiment 8\'s prepared positions; heavy rain and mud. Company C loses 37; Company B is drawn into a second ambush.','124',also=OP,place='a-bia',us=True,bnd='morning',words='"Sáng 12-5-1969" (the morning of May 12, 1969).',lw='A Bia: carpet bombing, Regiment 8 ambushes Company C')
E('abia17','1969-05-17','May 17','A Bia. The American command sends the 1st Battalion, 506th, up to take Hill 900; the rain holds it, and the attack stops again.','124',also=OP,place='a-bia',us=True,lw='A Bia: the 1st Battalion, 506th, sent to Hill 900')
E('abia19','1969-05-19','May 19','A Bia. Lt. Gen. Melvin Zais, the 101st Airborne\'s commander, orders the 2d Battalions of the 501st and 502d and the 2d Battalion, 3d Regiment, Saigon 1st Division, to encircle the mountain from northeast, southeast and southwest, to cut supply and retreat.','124–25',also=OP,place='a-bia',us=True,ntags=['name:zais-melvin'],names=['Zais'],lw='A Bia: Zais orders encirclement')
E('abia23','1969-05-23','May 23','A Bia. After 13 days and nights, short of food and ammunition and cut off from replacements, the Trị–Thiên forces withdraw. The history counts 1,500 of the 187th Brigade out of action and nearly a million pounds of bombs and shells on the defenders; its notes give American dead as 430 in a week (Amter) and 70 killed and 372 wounded in ten days (Pimlott). The troops call it Hamburger Hill.','125–26 and n. 1',also=OP,place='a-bia',us=True,check='the figures; the history gives its own and two American writers\' counts, VI, 125 n. 1.',lw='A Bia: the Trị–Thiên forces withdraw')
E('kennedy-abia','1969-05-21','May 21','Edward Kennedy on the assault on Hamburger Hill: immoral and senseless; American lives not to be spent for the army\'s pride.','126',th='vietnam-congress',polity='us',ntags=['name:kennedy-edward-m'],names=['Kennedy'],check='the day and the words; the history renders an AP story dated May 21, 1969 in Vietnamese, and the calendar\'s own record of the speech should be read.',lw='Kennedy on Hamburger Hill')
E('life-0627','1969-06-27','June 27','*Life* prints photographs of 241 Americans killed in a week\'s fighting; the history puts them at A Bia and says the public was angered and sickened.','126',th='vietnam',also=['press-and-broadcasting'],polity='us',check='the history\'s reading: the issue showed one week\'s dead in Vietnam, and the history ties it to A Bia.',ok=['ok:fields-place'],lw='Life prints 241 American dead')
E('sep4-pla','1969-09-04','Sept. 4','The Provisional Revolutionary Government, its Advisory Council, the National Liberation Front\'s Central Committee and the Alliance of National, Democratic and Peace Forces hold a joint conference on the memorial and mourning for Hồ Chí Minh. It cables the Party\'s Central Committee: the South pledges to fight on until the Americans leave and the Saigon regime falls.','134–35 and n. 1',also=['vietnam-paris'],ntags=['name:ho-chi-minh'],names=['Hồ Chí Minh'],see='cal.1969-09-02.vietnam-hanoi',ok=['ok:fields-place'], lw='Southern bodies hold joint conference for Hồ Chí Minh')
E('sep8-pla','1969-09-08','Sept. 8','The South\'s Provisional Revolutionary Government, the Front\'s Central Committee and the Alliance hold the memorial for Hồ Chí Minh and issue an appeal to the South\'s army and people to turn grief into strength.','135',also=['vietnam-paris'],ntags=['name:ho-chi-minh'],names=['Hồ Chí Minh'],see='cal.1969-09-08.vietnam-hanoi',lw='The South holds the memorial for Hồ Chí Minh')
C('cal.1969-09-04.vietnam-hanoi-4','136–37','the phase ends Sept. 15: tens of thousands out of action, hundreds of aircraft and thousands of vehicles destroyed, 193 vessels sunk or burned, 284 guns destroyed, by the history\'s count','D')
E('aug11-east','1969-08-11','Aug. 11','Eastern Nam Bộ, the autumn offensive\'s first night. The 7th Division\'s artillery hits a Saigon ranger camp at Lộc Ninh, 100 out of action; the command\'s sappers hit the Chơn Thành subsector and the Tếch Ních base of the Saigon 9th Regiment; the 5th Division\'s sappers the Bù Na ranger training camp and then the Bù Đăng subsector, three strategic hamlets broken. At Tây Ninh the 88th Regiment attacks an airborne group and fails, with heavy losses; sappers of the 1st Division\'s 2d Regiment take the Lôvêa cluster from the Saigon 2d Battalion, 8th Airborne, which falls back to Suối Dây.','131–32',also=OP,place='loc-ninh',us=False,bnd='night',see='cal.1969-08-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Aug. 11, eastern Nam Bộ: Lộc Ninh, Chơn Thành, Bù Na, Lôvêa')
E('aug12-r13','1969-08-12','Aug. 12','Route 13, Bình Long. At night Liberation forces ambush the Saigon 15th Armored Cavalry Regiment, many vehicles destroyed, six prisoners; the same day they destroy an American motorized group at Tân Khai and fight several ambushes west of Hớn Quản, three mechanized companies badly hurt.','131',also=OP,place='hon-quan',us=True,bnd='night',words='"đêm 12-8-1969" (the night of Aug. 12, 1969).',see='cal.1969-08-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Aug. 12: ambushes on Route 13')
E('aug11-r6','1969-08-11','Aug. 11','Binh Thuận, Region 6. Forces raid the Sông Mao base and badly hurt a battalion of the Saigon 44th Regiment; Saigon moves its reserves to Bình Thuận, and local forces ambush vehicles on Routes 1 and 20.','132–33',also=OP,place='song-mao',see='cal.1969-08-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Aug. 11, Region 6: Sông Mao raided',check='the place; the history names the province, Bình Thuận.')
E('aug12-bt','1969-08-12','Aug. 12–16','Bến Tre. The people and forces of Giồng Trôm, Mỏ Cày and Châu Thành combine attack and uprising, destroy pacification support forces and break some strategic hamlets. In the delta the artillery raids Mỹ Tho, Cai Lậy, Cái Bè, An Hữu and the Bình Đức base, and the Mỹ Tho commandos hit the Saigon 6th Armored Regiment\'s base. The history judges the phase\'s early stage weak.','133',also=OP,place='ben-tre',see='cal.1969-08-11.vietnam-hanoi',lw='Bến Tre, Aug. 12–16: attack and uprising',check='the days of the Mỹ Tho actions; the history gives the phase only.')
E('winter-pivot','1969-12','Dec., winter','The Miền command, at the start of the winter, decides to withdraw the main force of eastern Nam Bộ to the border for refit, leaving a few units, among them the 320th Regiment, to scatter and build guerrilla warfare among the hamlets.','141',also=OP,at='before 1969-12-21',vis=True,check='the day; the history gives the winter of 1969.',lw='Eastern Nam Bộ main forces pulled back to the border')
E('nov11-cl','1969-11-11','Nov. 11','Ô Môi, Long Mạnh canal, Long Tiên, Cai Lậy. Regiment 1 of Region 8 ambushes the Saigon 7th Division\'s 20th Battalion: hundreds killed or captured, 200 weapons taken; the local forces then break up nearly all the civil defense units in ten villages of Cai Lậy.','144',also=OP,place='long-tien-cai-lay',lw='Cai Lậy: Regiment 1 ambushes Saigon battalion')
E('nov-late-r8','1969-11','Nov., late','Mỹ Tho. Companies 1 and 3 of Battalion 514C ambush seven Civil Guard companies on Route 20; Company 2 raids at Chợ Bưng, Châu Thành, on Route 4: 17 pacification teams destroyed and 27 engineer vehicles. Region 8\'s task for the last months is set as breaking the pacification program.','144–45 and its note',also=OP,place='my-tho',at='before 1969-11-21',check='the days; the history gives "cuối tháng 11-1969".',lw='Mỹ Tho: Battalion 514C ambushes on Routes 20 and 4')
E('binhchanh','1969-11','Nov., late','Route 26. A sapper team under Lê Văn Phích brings down the Bình Chánh bridge, 100 meters, closing the road for two months.','146 and n. 1',also=OP,place='binh-chanh-bridge',at='before 1969-11-21',check='the province; the history does not name it.',lw='Bình Chánh bridge dropped on Route 26')
E('dec10-caibe','1969-12-10','Dec. 10','Cái Bè, Mỹ Tho. The Saigon 9th and 7th Divisions, four Ranger battalions and 20 heavy guns sweep west of Route 20 to Mỹ Thiện to break the base. Region 8, the province and district forces and the people fight on; at Hội Cư the province guard company hurts a company, at Hậu Mỹ Nam Battalion 216A another. After 15 days the sweep is called off.','145',also=OP,place='my-thien',lw='Cái Bè: a Saigon sweep west of Route 20')
E('delta-winter','1969-12','Dec., winter','Bến Tre, Kiến Phong, An Giang. Battalions 516 and 560 destroy two companies at Mỏ Cày and hurt a Civil Guard company at Minh Đức; local forces kill 48 pacification officials at Phước Hiệp and Định Thủy and 88 rural-development cadres at Thạnh Phú; Bến Tre\'s commandos set mines and grenades in the town, 147 killed. In Kiến Phong a battalion at Rạch Bà Lương stops a sweep; at Canal Ba a platoon under Tư Văn of 20 men holds off three attacks.','145–47',also=OP,place='ben-tre',at='before 1969-12-21',check='the days and the figures; the history gives the winter phase.',lw='The delta in the winter phase: Bến Tre, Kiến Phong')
E('bahon','1969-09-02','Sept. 2','Bà Hòn, Region 9. Ten Saigon battalions sweep the area; the Region\'s forces fight it off.','147',also=OP,place='ba-hon',check='the end of the sweep.',lw='Bà Hòn sweep, Region 9')
E('chuongthien','1969-09-19','Sept. 19','Chương Thiện, Region 9. Nine Saigon battalions and five river combat groups open a sweep; the Region\'s forces fight it off.','147',also=OP,place='chuong-thien',check='the end of the sweep.',lw='Chương Thiện sweep, Region 9')
